      "notes": "All claims are well-supported by their cited evidence. Tier assignments are appropriate: the \u00a32bn/year revenue cost is correctly labelled measurable (it is a published Resolution Foundation estimate of the 2022 repeal cost, a close proxy). The 30% take-home pay reduction is correctly labelled projected. The mixed direction is genuinely supported by claims on both sides (upside for contractors, downside for public finances and lower-income households). The magnitude/time_horizon/direction combination is internally consistent. No lever leakage: the analysis is anchored to disposable income and cost-of-living effects, not IR35 policy on its own merits. No party-blind issues detected. One minor note: E9 (Resolution Foundation) is advocacy-adjacent institutional source and is the sole basis for the \u00a32bn/year cost figure; this is flagged as a warning but not blocking given the institutional standing of the Resolution Foundation and corroboration from E6 (\u00a36.19bn over five years for the full repeal, consistent in magnitude)."
